{
  "id": "LeadLoomIntake01",
  "name": "LeadLoom: lead intake",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## LeadLoom: lead intake\nThree ways in: the website form, inbound email (Postmark's JSON) and bookings (Cal.com, signed).\n\nn8n does the plumbing: it receives each event, forwards the raw body to the LeadLoom service, answers the sender, routes on the service's decision, waits for a person when the lead is unsure, and sends the Slack alert. The service (Python) checks signatures, dedupes, enriches, scores, and writes HubSpot, each step idempotent and audited.\n\nConfig comes from env: `LEADLOOM_API_URL`, `LEADLOOM_API_KEY`, `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL`.",
        "width": 760,
        "height": 260,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "19560826-3dc2-57a0-b345-361d762965c3",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -380
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Retry\nThe review page's Retry button (and an approval whose wait has expired) re-enters here. Qualify is idempotent: it returns the lead's next step.",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 140,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "2d6e9f3e-e1af-5e4b-a6f4-f7ac39416f0f",
